  "protocol": {
    "design": "Fresh counterbalanced off/on ordinary matches, eight adjacent order-pairs on each of dm2 and dm4, 60 seconds each, skill 1. All scheduled tapes retained. Native brief supplies every gameplay metric. Primary endpoint is completed-goal rate per match-minute, not selections or touches.",
    "equivalence": "Two one-sided tests at alpha .05: paired mean difference 90% Student-t CI must lie strictly inside [-2,+2] goals per match-minute on EACH map. This rules out the pilot-sized approximately four-goal/minute deficit, not arbitrarily small effects. No significance/non-significance shortcut. No optional stopping within this cohort.",
    "timing": "Common BHVTIME probe in all arms, five-second windows; discard first window. Mean frame-time on-minus-off 90% paired CI within +/-1 ms; no material excess >50 ms frames. Direct process CPU and bytes recorded separately. Native tick classes reported; no cross-class native verdict asserted.",
    "mechanism": "Separate exploratory arms: off, compute-only 591, original fragmented output 592, batched output 590. Two 60-second runs each per map, counterbalanced. Mechanism does not contribute to confirmatory gameplay equivalence cohort.",
    "secondary": "Report grabs, acquisitions, engages, stalls, frags, lava, freezes, average speed and per-map effects. A contradictory signal blocks claiming broad gameplay equivalence even if primary passes.",
    "controls": "Same pinned source/binary/nav, normal isolated lab matches, no BHVFIX, developer 1, scratch1 591 common cadence probe; diagnostics only scratch4 differs. Retain errors and exclusions. No perception edits. Run source noninterference audit and actual scheduled-call guards after fixes."
  },
  "mechanism_amendment": {
    "reason": "The fixed 32-tape cohort completed with cadence equivalence but inconclusive goal equivalence, and gameplay variation confounded process CPU. Replace the exploratory free-running mechanism runs with identical-input engine replays; do not reinterpret the primary confidence intervals as passes.",
    "inputs": "Private source copies only: common 16-bit integer QC input generator (all intermediate integers exactly representable), vanilla host_framerate=0.015625, end after 3842 frames. Seeds 113 and 50917 on both dm2 and dm4, selected before the holdout cases. Original production RNG is unchanged.",
    "arms": "Candidate off, repeated off, compute-only 591, fragmented 592, batched 590. Then a private copy of the saved original source using the same input provider and frame steps. Disabled repeats must match before other arms can pass.",
    "acceptance": "Byte-identical exported gameplay records and entity dumps, excluding only ar_bd_* diagnostic fields. Final RNG state/call count and completed-goal counters are included. Maximum 600 edicts. At least one positive consumed-goal case per map across the selected inputs; zero-goal cases remain valid negative controls. Native briefs remain the metric authority.",
    "cost": "On remaining cases only, capture process CPU over the first approximately 50 seconds after the acknowledged map reset. Same simulated gameplay workload in each arm. Descriptive overhead measurement, separate from the fixed real-time statistical cohort.",
    "limits": "Fixed-input replay is functional noninterference evidence, not a replacement for real-time statistical equivalence. Text entity dumps round floating values. Keep the real-time goal finding inconclusive if its pre-registered bounds fail. Perception remains unchanged."
  },
